       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, or prolonged vasodilatory shock. Overdoses of this size have caused refractory shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nCan you confirm what you intended? Possible explanations include:\n\n- **A typo:** the intended dose may have been 5 mg, which is the usual starting dose, or 10 mg, which is the maximum.\n- **A unit or drug mix-up:** the order may have been meant for a different medication.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away. For example, I can enter amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily. If you really do want 50 mg, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. I'd suggest pharmacy verification in that case."
